%% Pudel Admin Mutual Authentication Flow v2.5.0
%% Server proves identity with Ed25519 (keys/pv.key), each admin proves identity
%% with their own RSA keypair. The resulting AdminJWT is DPoP-bound and stored in
%% dpop_keys.admin_token — it is never returned to the browser.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Admin User
    participant Browser as Browser (Vue)
    participant API as AdminController
    participant Filter as JwtAuthenticationFilter
    participant KeyMgr as DPoPKeyManager
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Discord as Discord OAuth2

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 1: Discord OAuth login (cookie session required first)

    Admin->>Browser: Click "Login with Discord"
    Browser->>Discord: Redirect to OAuth2
    Discord->>Admin: Consent screen
    Admin->>Discord: Approve
    Discord->>Browser: Redirect with code
    Browser->>API: POST /api/auth/discord/callback (Cookie: pudel_session)
    API->>Discord: Exchange code for tokens
    Discord-->>API: User info (id, username)
    API->>DB: Store DPoP-bound user JWT in dpop_keys.access_token
    API-->>Browser: { accessToken: null, user, tokenType: "COOKIE" }
    Note right of Browser: Nothing to store — the HttpOnly cookie is the credential

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 2: Check admin eligibility

    Admin->>Browser: Click "Admin Portal"
    Browser->>Filter: GET /api/admin/check (cookie only)
    Filter->>Filter: Authenticate cookie session<br/>request attr pudel.session.keyId
    Filter-->>API: Authentication(principal = discordUserId, [DPOP_VERIFIED])
    API->>DB: SELECT admin_whitelist WHERE discord_user_id = ?
    alt In whitelist and enabled
        DB-->>API: Admin entry
        API-->>Browser: { isAdmin: true, isAdminSession: false,<br/>adminRole, canModify, canManageAdmins, hasPublicKey }
    else Not in whitelist / disabled
        API-->>Browser: { isAdmin: false, reason: "..." }
        Browser-->>Admin: Access Denied
    end

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 3: Request challenge (server proves identity)

    Admin->>Browser: Click "Request Challenge"
    Browser->>API: GET /api/admin/challenge
    API->>API: Load Ed25519 keys (jwtUtil.getPrivateKey/getPublicKey)
    API->>API: challengeId = UUID, nonce = UUID, expiry = now + 60s
    API->>API: Sign challenge JWT with EdDSA
    Note right of API: sub=pudel-admin-challenge,<br/>claims: challengeId, nonce, timestamp
    API->>API: pendingChallenges[challengeId] = ChallengeData<br/>(in-memory, swept every 60s)
    API-->>Browser: { challengeId, nonce, timestamp, expiry, signature }

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 4: Verify server identity (optional)

    Browser->>Browser: GET /api/admin/public-key -> { publicKey, algorithm: "EdDSA" }
    Browser->>Browser: Verify challenge signature with that public key
    Browser-->>Admin: "Server identity verified"

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 5: Admin signs the nonce (RSA)

    Admin->>Browser: Provide RSA private key (stays in browser)
    Browser->>Browser: SHA256withRSA_sign(nonce, adminPrivateKey)
    Note right of Browser: signature = Base64(SHA256withRSA(nonce))
    Browser-->>Admin: "Challenge signed"

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 6: Submit signed challenge

    Admin->>Browser: Click "Complete Login"
    Browser->>API: POST /api/admin/auth/mutual (cookie only)<br/>Body: { challengeId, signature }
    API->>API: browserKeyId = request attr pudel.session.keyId
    API->>DB: SELECT dpop_keys WHERE key_id = browserKeyId
    API->>API: presentedThumbprint = KeyMgr.getPublicKeyThumbprint(browserKeyId)
    API->>API: discordUserId must match ^\d{17,19}$
    API->>API: pendingChallenges.remove(challengeId) and reject if absent/expired
    API->>DB: SELECT public_key_pem FROM admin_whitelist
    API->>API: KeyFactory("RSA") from PEM
    API->>API: SHA256withRSA_verify(nonce, signature, adminPublicKey)

    alt Signature valid
        API->>API: jwtUtil.generateDPoPBoundToken("pudel-admin-session",<br/>{ sessionId, discordUserId, discordUsername,<br/>adminRole, canModify, canManageAdmins }, presentedThumbprint)
        Note right of API: EdDSA signed, cnf.jkt = browser session thumbprint.<br/>ADMIN_SESSION_EXPIRY_MS = 1 hour.
        API->>KeyMgr: storeAdminToken(browserKeyId, adminToken)
        KeyMgr->>DB: UPDATE dpop_keys SET admin_token = …
        API->>DB: UPDATE admin_whitelist SET last_login = NOW()
        API->>Browser: Set-Cookie pudel-swagger-session=<adminToken><br/>HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure when X-Forwarded-Proto=https
        API-->>Browser: { success: true, discordUserId, adminRole,<br/>canModify, canManageAdmins, expiresAt, expiresIn: 3600 }
        Note right of Browser: No adminToken in the body — nothing to store in JS
    else Not whitelisted / disabled / no key / bad signature
        API-->>Browser: 403 or 401 { error: "..." }
    end

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 7: Admin operations (cookie + DB-backed admin token)

    Admin->>Browser: Manage plugins
    Browser->>Filter: GET /api/admin/plugins (cookie only)
    Filter-->>API: Authenticated request + pudel.session.keyId
    API->>API: validateAdminSession(authHeader)
    Note right of API: Ignores the header. Loads dpop_keys.admin_token<br/>for the current browser key, verifies EdDSA signature,<br/>requires sub=pudel-admin-session and a non-expired exp.<br/>An expired token is cleared from the row.
    alt Valid admin session
        API-->>Browser: { plugins: [...], total, enabled }
    else No/expired admin token
        API-->>Browser: 401 { error: "Invalid or missing admin token" }
    end

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 8: Live log stream over WebSocket

    Admin->>Browser: Open log viewer
    Browser->>API: WS handshake /ws/admin/logs (cookie travels with handshake)
    API->>API: AdminLogHandshakeInterceptor.beforeHandshake
    Note right of API: Allowed origins = pudel.cors.allowed-origins (strict).<br/>Reads cookie -> dpop_keys.admin_token -> validateToken +<br/>sub/expiry checks. Rejects with 401 otherwise.
    API-->>Browser: 101 Switching Protocols
    API-->>Browser: log entries pushed over the socket

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 9: Swagger UI access (separate cookie)

    Admin->>Browser: Open API docs
    Browser->>API: POST /api/admin/swagger/authorize (cookie only)
    API->>API: Requires a valid admin session
    API->>Browser: Set-Cookie pudel-swagger-session (subject pudel-swagger-session, 1h, SameSite=Lax)
    Browser->>API: GET /swagger-ui.html
    API->>API: SwaggerAccessFilter checks the swagger cookie
    API-->>Browser: Swagger UI
    Note right of API: DELETE /api/admin/swagger/authorize clears it.<br/>Query-parameter tokens (?swaggerToken=…) exist only when<br/>pudel.swagger.allow-query-token=true, and expire after 30s.

    Note over Admin,Discord: Step 10: Logout

    Admin->>Browser: Click "Logout"
    Browser->>API: POST /api/admin/logout (cookie only)
    API->>KeyMgr: clearAdminToken(browserKeyId)
    KeyMgr->>DB: UPDATE dpop_keys SET admin_token = NULL
    Note right of KeyMgr: The browser session itself stays alive
    API-->>Browser: { message: "Logged out successfully" }